+`registerBrowserAuthentication` installs one lifecycle-owned browser authentication provider. While installed, it replaces the startup-token cookie exchange for index requests, HTTP APIs, and WebSocket admission; Host and Origin checks still run first. A second provider is rejected, and disposal restores native authentication.
+
